### Execution host and tool spelling

Keep every workflow step, authority check, hold and reporting requirement below.
The execution host determines how to invoke those operations:

- With Claude Code, use the native Bash, Read and skill invocations shown below.
- With the Pydantic executor, use its finite typed tools. Every native tool,
  shell paging or slash-skill example below denotes the corresponding operation
  in this mapping; it does not grant a shell or a second way around a refusal.
  Invoke one canonical command per `run_cs(argv=[...])`, omitting the
  `.venv/bin/python -m cs` launcher prefix. Use `--json` for identity,
  configuration, tasks and other reads that support it. For example,
  `run_cs(argv=["whoami", "--json"])`. Keep command arguments separate;
  never include shell operators, wrappers, redirects or background execution.
- Invoke `load_workflow(name="cs-triage-mail")` or the other named rendered
  skill in place of a slash-skill call. Read its complete current content.
  Use `read_context(path=..., offset=..., length=...)` for referenced permitted
  clone context, and `pause_status()` for the pause check. A paused result
  means stop under the same workflow rule.
- Use `read_artifact(artifact_id=..., offset=..., length=...)` for artifacts
  returned by this run, instead of native Read or `dd`. Follow the actual
  returned byte intervals through EOF, respecting their encoding, hashes and
  total length. Keep every byte; never invent an artifact ID or use an older
  run. Complete the semantic inventory and paired envelope, including tasks
  and review, before effects. Retained raw output is not a second mandatory
  inventory read when the complete current projection is already delivered.
- The executor owns command deadlines and serial execution. Do not reproduce
  native timeout/background parameters as command arguments. Preserve actual
  exit, stderr, source-bound holds and unresolved effects. A refusal is not
  permission to retry, substitute a shell or skip required evidence.

Tool delivery proves transport only. Complete the same inspection, selection
and business work, and distinguish a held or failed run from completion.

